// Package propose turns the planner's proposals into branches and pull
// requests. It never edits a lock file itself and never runs a package
// manager on the server: manifests are changed as text, and the lock file is
// regenerated by the ecosystem's own tool inside a step container (the same
// executor runners use), in a copy of the files without Git metadata, with no
// secrets and only the registries the installation allows. The server then
// takes back only the files that were supposed to change (a manifest, its
// lock file) and refuses anything else, commits them to the updater's own
// branch, and opens or updates a pull request. A person (or the pipeline's
// checks) decides what happens next.
package propose
